		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=5787#p5787"><![CDATA[
See image at: <a href="http://savefile.com/download/1110356?PHPSESSID=274a27bdc49465910876993a2c389af9" class="postlink">http://savefile.com/download/1110356?PH ... 3a2c389af9</a><br><br>What happened is you baked into IPO, cleared IPO, then baked again, multiple objects had the same IPO, bad.<br><br>Unfoutunatly, you need to delete any objects that you made after the first bake into ipo test. Then, follow the image's instructions every time you start up blender and you will be safe to duplicate oblects (just clear the ipo's first).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1492">fast solve</a> — Tue Oct 09, 2007 4:02 am</p><hr />
