		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Auto-Deleting Objects after IPO Baking]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=5060#p5060"><![CDATA[
I built some sort of Rube Goldberg machine in Blender, using Bullet pysics and IPO baking.<br><br>When doing the first, small version of the machine everythin worked.<br><br>Now, as I expanded the machine, the IPO Recorder deletes some of my dynamic objects as soon as the IPO baking finishes. Everything works, as long as I just do the realtime simulation, only the IPO baking is affected.<br><br>If I remove some of the objects before doing the IPO baking, the remaining are handled right.<br>So is there a limit of dynamic objects when using IPO baking?<br>I assume there are about 30-50 of them ATM.<br><br>/FilE<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1886">FilE</a> — Fri Aug 17, 2007 2:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
